  m_Name: Object_10
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Sensor
  description: The Sensor, situated at the middle-center-rear of the engine, is a
    tiny, compact, plastic-cone-black component that monitors and reports critical
    engine parameters, such as temperature and pressure. Its small size and compact
    shape enable it to fit in tight spaces, while its plastic-cone-black material
    provides sufficient durability and resistance to environmental factors. Interestingly,
    the Sensor's position at the rear of the engine allows it to provide real-time
    data to the engine control system, enabling optimal engine performance and efficiency.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
